<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE task PUBLIC "-//OASIS//DTD DITA Task//EN" "task.dtd">
<task id="add-a-repository" xml:lang="en-GB">
  <title>Add a repository</title>
  <shortdesc>Record an archive, a library or a museum that keeps the records you use, so a source can point to it.</shortdesc>
  <prolog>
    <critdates>
      <created date="2026-11-10"/>
    </critdates>
    <metadata>
      <audience type="user" experiencelevel="novice"/>
      <category>How-to</category>
      <keywords>
        <keyword>archive</keyword>
        <keyword>library</keyword>
        <keyword>museum</keyword>
        <keyword>where a record is held</keyword>
      </keywords>
    </metadata>
    <resourceid appname="ufti" appid="repositories.edit"/>
  </prolog>
  <taskbody>
    <context>
      <p>A repository is a place that keeps records: an archive, a library, a website or a family collection. A source can point to the place that holds it. This page adds the Brontë Parsonage Museum.</p>
    </context>
    <steps>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-where-records-are-kept"/> in the menu.</cmd>
        <stepresult>
          <p>The page lists the places you have recorded. Each has a name and an address.</p>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-add"/>.</cmd>
        <stepresult>
          <p>The list named <uicontrol keyref="ui-add-a-record"/> opens.</p>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-repository"/> in the part named <uicontrol keyref="ui-add-to-the-workspace"/>, then choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-add-button"/>.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>The list scrolls. Turn the mouse wheel with the pointer on it to find the part.</p>
        </info>
        <stepresult>
          <p>A form opens.</p>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>In <uicontrol keyref="ui-name"/>, type <userinput>Brontë Parsonage Museum, the Brontë Society</userinput>.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>Only this box is needed.</p>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>In <uicontrol keyref="ui-address"/>, type <userinput>Church Street, Haworth</userinput>.</cmd>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Under <uicontrol keyref="ui-telephone-email-website"/>, choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-add-row"/>.</cmd>
        <stepresult>
          <p>A row appears with a list named <uicontrol keyref="ui-kind"/> and a box named <uicontrol keyref="ui-number-or-address"/>.</p>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose the kind that fits, then type the website in <uicontrol keyref="ui-number-or-address"/>.</cmd>
        <info>
          <p>For this museum, type <userinput>https://www.bronte.org.uk/</userinput>.</p>
        </info>
      </step>
      <step>
        <cmd>Choose <uicontrol keyref="ui-save"/>.</cmd>
        <stepresult>
          <p>The page <uicontrol keyref="ui-where-records-are-kept"/> shows the museum with its address. Each place has <uicontrol keyref="ui-edit"/> and <uicontrol keyref="ui-delete"/>, and a count of its notes.</p>
          <fig>
            <image keyref="img-repositories"/>
          </fig>
        </stepresult>
      </step>
    </steps>
    <result>
      <p>The place is in the list. Add the others the same way, such as The National Archives at Kew.</p>
    </result>
    <postreq>
      <p>Next: <xref keyref="add-a-source"/>.</p>
    </postreq>
  </taskbody>
</task>
